  "scope": "Fresh Lean ordinary-source and independently reviewed packages exercise the copied Window check inside Booking and the owned Claim check across Ticket resources. Full packages cover borrowed and transferred inputs, leased results, exact constructor rejection before transfer, synchronous host callbacks, invalid explicit recovery before callback entry, returned Lean closures, exception identity and cleanup. Standalone result-only packages expose Lean-produced proof-free Claim results without checked inputs, transfer or callback metadata. Every route reproduces Composer API, npm component and npm shared-runtime archives, removes author/build roots, installs offline, physically relocates the installed tree and passes eight Node plus eight Chromium startup/lazy weak/strict executions with zero live identities and later-request recovery. This local evidence covers the tested acyclic Booking, Window and Claim shapes, the quota bound and synchronous callbacks only. It does not establish recursive owned graphs, retained or asynchronous callbacks, other predicates, dispatch counts, peak memory or hosted acceptance. The pinned PHP-Wasm runtime, browser and external compiler distributions remain trusted inputs represented by recorded identities.",
